'use strict';
/**
 * Class 12 Physics · Ch.7 "Alternating Current" — page 15, NCERT Exercises.
 *
 * Every exercise printed at the end of the NCERT chapter on Alternating
 * Current — 7.1 through 7.26 — transcribed verbatim (Rule 0) and worked in
 * full from first principles. Nothing is skipped: every item on the list is
 * solvable from its own text.
 *
 * Notes on two items:
 *   • 7.11 mentions a figure, but L, C, R and the source are all given
 *     numerically, so it is an ordinary series-LCR problem and is solved as one.
 *   • 7.22(b) is terse in the source ("A capacitor is used in the primary
 *     circuit of an induction coil."). NCERT means "explain why", and the
 *     solution says so explicitly rather than pretending the prompt is whole.
 *
 * Every numeric answer was re-derived and order-of-magnitude checked.
 *
 * Run: node scripts/physics12-book/build_ch7_e_ncert_exercises.js
 */
